        <h1>LeetCode 1927: Sum Game (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Alice and Bob play a game on a string of digits and '?' characters. On each turn, a player replaces a
                '?' with any digit 1-9. Alice wants the sum of the first half to not equal the second half; Bob wants
                them equal. Alice goes first and both play optimally. Return true if Alice wins.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: num = "5023"<br>
                Output: false<br>
                Explanation: The first half sum is 5+0=5 and the second half is 2+3=5. Since they are already equal and
                no '?' exists, Bob wins by default (no moves needed), so Alice loses.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    bool sumGame(string str) {
        double diff = 0;
        double len = str.length();
        for (int idx = 0; idx &lt; len; idx++) {
            double sign = (idx &lt; len / 2) ? 1 : -1;
            double val = (str[idx] == '?') ? 4.5 : str[idx] - '0';
            diff += sign * val;
        }
        return diff != 0.0;
    }
};</code></pre>
